BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:IM4agdQ1FN2QTG5JR1Qgc
SUMMARY:Influencer–Brand Partnerships: A Matching Approach
DTSTAMP:20260730T054954Z
DTSTART:20260803T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Masoud Jabbari  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis De
	fense  Department: Economics  Location: Kraft Hall 102  This thesis studie
	s how brands allocate advertising budgets across bundles of Instagram infl
	uencers in a centralized platform\, addressing the business problem of pla
	tform assignment potentially overriding brand preferences. I develop a str
	uctural matching model to recover preferences over influencer scale\, enga
	gement\, and thematic focus\, estimated conditional on campaign characteri
	stics using administrative platform data. Preferences are identified using
	 pairwise stability\, first in matches alone and then jointly in matches a
	nd prices\, leveraging influencer posted prices and a control-function app
	roach based on hedonic regressions to address price endogeneity and persis
	tent unobserved quality. The estimates indicate that follower count is mos
	t valuable for follower-growth campaigns\, whereas engagement and thematic
	 concentration become relatively more important for sales- and lead-genera
	tion objectives. Counterfactual analyses highlight the important role of N
	ano and Micro influencers in maintaining brand utility and demonstrate tha
	t platform assignments in CPM campaigns can be substantially improved when
	 aligned with estimated preferences. Methodologically\, this thesis demons
	trates how preferences can be recovered in platform-mediated matching envi
	ronments with limited choice-set observability\, providing a tractable fra
	mework for analyzing digital advertising markets and informing more effect
	ive platform allocation design.  &#160\;  (Department : Economics)\n\nhttp
	s://events.rice.edu/live/events/435072-influencerbrand-partnerships-a-matc
	hing-approach\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/435072-influencerbrand-partnerships
	-a-matching-approach
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Kraft Hall
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
